.TH "RAPTOR-DECLASSIFY" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-declassify \- write a share\-safe copy with names/notes removed
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor declassify\fR [\-h] [\-\-annotations {keep,text,all}] [\-\-keep\-names] [\-\-keep\-comments] [\-\-keep\-metadata] [\-\-keep\-advisor] [\-\-keep\-rates] MODEL OUTPUT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write a declassified .rbds: element names become type labels, and comments, chosen annotations, project metadata, rate names/formulas and Advisor notes can be removed. IDs, links and data are kept.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-annotations\fR \fI{keep|text|all}\fR
remove no annotations, text only, or every shape
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-names\fR
keep element and hierarchy names
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-comments\fR
keep element comments
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-metadata\fR
keep the print title block and project preferences
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-advisor\fR
keep the reasons attached to dismissed Advisor findings
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-rates\fR
keep the rate library and field formulas
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
